Negative control for the FE-3113 capability spec (`AC5` · `S13`).

`canErrorCollection` is the claim that this module recorded a REFUSAL — a status
staging actually returned. The mutant claims it for any module holding a
recording at all, which is the dead-alive shape the story deleted: a module with
nothing failing on record is reported able to serve a forced failure, the picker
offers it, arming it serves the read exactly as recorded, and the page never
changes.

What must go red is provenance, not the flag's shape. `failure` stays undefined
under the mutant, so an assertion that only reads the booleans, or that mirrors
`corpusCapabilities`' own derivation back at it, passes and proves nothing.
Derive the expectation independently from `request.method` and
`response.status`, and require the carried `failure` to be one of the module's
OWN recordings.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the capability spec — a capability is TRUE only when a recording backs it.

